<title>USA: LPC-Bankers look to fund SuperMercados Norte's LBO.</title>
<headline>LPC-Bankers look to fund SuperMercados Norte's LBO.</headline>
<text>
<p>NEW YORK, Sept 10 (LPC) - Banks are bidding on the roughly $400 million leveraged buyout (LBO) of Argentine retail concern Supermercados Norte by Argentine LBO firm Exxel, market sources said.</p>
<p>The deal will be made up of equity, bonds and bank debt, the sources added.</p>
<p>Chase Manhattan, Merrill Lynch and Co Inc, and Donaldson, Lufkin and Jenrette Corp, among others, are bidding on the deal, sources said.</p>
<p>Supermercados Norte is the largest supermarket chain in Argentina.</p>
<p>-- Meredith Coffey, LPC Editorial, 212-489-5455</p>
</text>
